    "seed": 1031,
    "walkthrough": {
      "steps": [
        "Add an Application Load Balancer and connect Customers to it. Delete the direct Customers → web server connection.",
        "Change the existing server to t3.medium in AZ A, and add a second t3.medium in AZ B.",
        "Connect the load balancer to both servers, and both servers to the database.",
        "Run the day and watch the lunchtime crash."
      ],
      "why": "When one server dies, the load balancer’s health checks send everyone to the other within a minute. Each t3.medium can carry the full load alone (about 84% at peak), so availability stays above 99.9%, and two t3.medium cost about the same as one c7g.large."
    }
